# ── LOCAL WORKING DROPS — reference material, never source (Stuart 2026-09-15) ────────────────
# Spreadsheets, drawings, CAD and render dumps that arrive by email and get worked on beside the
# repo: ~440MB across these folders, which would sit in the history forever (and GitHub refuses a
# file over 100MB). They are inputs to work, not the work. Anything the app actually READS is in
# src/ — e.g. the NetSuite item field map was transcribed from Items_NS/ into
# src/components/Shared/nsItemFields.js, which is why that folder can go.
#
# EVERY PATTERN IS ANCHORED WITH A LEADING SLASH, ON PURPOSE. A bare "SpecSheet/" would match at
# ANY depth and would ignore src/components/SpecSheet/ — the live spec-sheet feature (S6's
# territory, 8 tracked files). Keep the slash. Same reason for /Fabricut/ and /H2/.
/0903/
/DOUBLE/
/Fabricut/
/Fabricut GLB/
/Finishes_Combo/
/H2/
/Items_NS/
/July28/
/July29/
/July 30/
/Spec Sheets/
/SpecSheet/
